store_head replaces the head without raising head_generation_, so a reset
to an older state (a failed flush's, resume()'s) leaves the paths found in
the dropped head usable on a tree that does not descend from it (#754).
Guarded-by: "write paths: a plan prepared in a head that resume() dropped goes by key"

diff --git a/bytecaskdb/bytecask.cppm b/bytecaskdb/bytecask.cppm
index 8a641099..38afb2be 100644
--- a/bytecaskdb/bytecask.cppm
+++ b/bytecaskdb/bytecask.cppm
@@ -1829,7 +1829,6 @@ private:
   void store_head(std::shared_ptr<EngineState> s) {
     const auto replaced = std::atomic_exchange(&head_, std::move(s));
     if (replaced == nullptr) return;  // the first head
-    head_generation_.fetch_add(1);
   }
 #pragma clang diagnostic pop
 
